        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by incorrect command generation for checking whether a process is alive and for sending signals to processes on certain Linux distributions. The previous implementation did not account for variations in command syntax and the necessity of using bash for these operations, leading to failures in executing the shell-kill command properly.

        Commit message:
        HADOOP-12441. Fixed shell-kill command behaviour to work
 correctly on some Linux distributions after HADOOP-12317. Contributed by
 Wangda Tan.  

